"**Answer: Taiwan**  \n\n**Why?**\n\n| Country (top 5 by\u202fGovernment\u2011Spending score) | U.S. State Department Travel\u2011Advisory level (Feb\u202f2024) |\n|---------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|\n| Singapore | Level\u202f1 \u2013 \u201cExercise Normal Precautions\u201d |\n| Switzerland | Level\u202f1 \u2013 \u201cExercise Normal Precautions\u201d |\n| Ireland | Level\u202f1 \u2013 \u201cExercise Normal Precautions\u201d |\n| **Taiwan** | **Level\u202f4 \u2013 \u201cDo Not Travel\u201d** |\n| Luxembourg | Level\u202f1 \u2013 \u201cExercise Normal Precautions\u201d |\n\nWith the travel\u2011advisory system, Level\u202f4 represents the highest degree of caution (\u201cDo\u202fNot\u202fTravel\u201d). Among the top\u2011five countries on the Heritage Foundation\u2019s Government\u2011Spending ranking (Singapore, Switzerland, Ireland, Taiwan, Luxembourg), **Taiwan is the only one that, as of February\u202f2024, carried a Level\u202f4 warning**. All the others retained a Level\u202f1 designation, indicating normal preventive precautions."